module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.IteratedMvPolynomial
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.ClosedPoint.Regular
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.NaiveCotangent.ConormalSurjection
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.NaiveCotangent
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.NaiveCotangent.BaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.NaiveCotangent.DegreeZeroRow
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.Lifting
import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Algebraization

/-!
# The combined presentation of Stacks 0ALM: `A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ B⟨y⟩` with kernel `J·A⟨x, y⟩`

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal and `B` an object of (Stacks 0AL4) with a
completed polynomial presentation `B = A⟨x₁, …, x_r⟩ / J`.  The proof of **Stacks 0ALM**
combines that presentation with a presentation `C = B⟨y₁, …, y_s⟩ / J'` of a `B`-object into
a single presentation `C = A⟨x, y⟩ / K`.  The step which makes this possible, and which does
not mention `C` at all, is the surjection

```
π : A⟨x₁, …, x_r, y₁, …, y_s⟩  ↠  B⟨y₁, …, y_s⟩,      ker π = J · A⟨x, y⟩,
```

and this file constructs it.  Given it, the combined presentation is `Q.toAlgHom ∘ π` for any
presentation `Q` of `C` over `B`, its kernel `K` is the preimage of `J'`, and the degree-`1`
row of the transitivity diagram is
`Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.exact_liftBaseChange_map_of_ker_eq` applied to the two
morphisms of extensions.

The construction is a composition of three identifications, none of which needs a diagram
chase:

* `A⟨x, y⟩ ≅ (A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩`, which is `AdicCompletion.finIteratedMvPolynomialAlgEquiv`;
* `(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩ ⧸ J·(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩ ≅ (A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y])^∧`, which is
  `adicCompletionQuotientAlgEquiv` — this is where exactness of `I`-adic completion on
  finite modules over the Noetherian ring `A⟨x⟩[y]` (Stacks 00MA, 00MB) enters;
* `A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y] ≅ B[y]`, which is `MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial`.

Because the last two are isomorphisms and the middle one is a quotient map, both the
surjectivity of `π` and the computation of its kernel are immediate: `ker π` is the preimage
under the first identification of the ideal generated by `J`.

## Main definitions

* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedInclusion` — the inclusion
  `A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩` of the first `r` variables.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedProjection` — the surjection
  `π : A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ B⟨y⟩`.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.outerPolynomialMap` — the polynomial map
  `A[x, y] → B[y]` of which `π` is the completion.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.innerBaseChangeDifferential`,
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedDifferential` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.outerDifferential` — the three degree-`0` differentials
  of the diagram of Stacks 0ALM, those of `NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C`, `NL^∧_{C/A}` and `NL^∧_{C/B}`.

## Main results

* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.ker_eq_ideal` — the kernel of a presentation is its
  ideal. Proved in `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.Lifting`, which this module re-exports.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedProjection_surjective` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.ker_combinedProjection` — **`π` is surjective with
  kernel `J · A⟨x, y⟩`**.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedInclusion_of_X` — the inclusion is the
  expected one: it sends `xᵢ` to `xᵢ`, and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedProjection_of_X_natAdd` — `π` sends `yⱼ` to
  `yⱼ`.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.partialDeriv_combinedInclusion`,
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.partialDeriv_natAdd_combinedInclusion` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.partialDeriv_combinedProjection` — **the three
  `partialDeriv` compatibilities of Stacks 0ALM**, which are the two commuting squares of its
  diagram in degree `0`.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedInclusion_eq` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedProjection_eq` — **both maps are induced maps
  of adic completions**, namely the completions of the renaming `A[x] → A[x, y]` and of
  `outerPolynomialMap`; hence
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.continuous_combinedInclusion` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.continuous_combinedProjection`, **both maps are
  continuous** for the inverse-limit topologies, which is what the uniqueness of the formal
  partial derivatives needs.

* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedDifferential_comp_innerCotangentMap` and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.outerDifferential_comp_outerCotangentMap` — **the two
  commuting squares of Stacks 0ALM**.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.exists_sixTerm_exact_combined` — **the six-term exact
  sequence of Stacks 0ALM**.
* `Rig.tensorProductH0Equiv` — **`H⁰` commutes with base change**, with no hypotheses, and
  `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.innerBaseChangeH0Equiv` its specialization to 0ALM's
  `H⁰` entry, which recovers the source display's `C ⊗_B H⁰(NL^∧_{B/A})` spelling by name.
  Both untagged: an identification used in reading 0ALM, not part of its covering set.

## Implementation notes

`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.ker_eq_ideal` was proved here as well as in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.Lifting`, under the same fully-qualified name and with a type
equal to the byte, so in any environment holding both modules the two were one constant and
this file's proof was silently discarded on import. The copy here has been removed and
`Rig.Lifting` is imported above instead: it is the side the import order already selected, it
carries the keys 0GAP "the lifting claim" and 0AK6 while the duplicate itself was untagged on
both sides, and its own import closure is the smaller of the two by an order of magnitude —
thirty-five own-library modules against this file's three hundred and seventy-nine. The edge
therefore runs from the heavy module to the light one; the reverse direction would have added
three hundred and fifty-nine modules to `Rig.Lifting`'s closure and to that of everything
below it. Neither module reaches the other, so no cycle is created, and this module has no
importers, so the fifteen modules the edge adds to its closure reach nothing further. Nothing
stopped being proved — the statement is unchanged and is settled by a bare application of the
`Rig.Lifting` theorem in either direction.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ALM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ALM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AJP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AJP)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial

namespace Rig

namespace CompletedPolynomialPresentation

universe u v

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A} {B : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
  (P : CompletedPolynomialPresentation I B)

section Combined

variable [IsNoetherianRing A] (s : ℕ)

/-- The polynomial algebra `A⟨x⟩[y₁, …, y_s]` in the outer variables over the completed
polynomial algebra in the inner ones. -/
public abbrev outerPolynomial := MvPolynomial (Fin s) P.completedPolynomialRing

/-- The ideal `J · A⟨x⟩[y]` of `A⟨x⟩[y]` generated by the ideal of the presentation. -/
public abbrev outerIdeal : Ideal (P.outerPolynomial s) :=
  P.ideal.map (algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerPolynomial s))

/-- `A⟨x⟩` is Noetherian, hence so is `A⟨x⟩[y₁, …, y_s]`. -/
public instance isNoetherianRing_outerPolynomial : IsNoetherianRing (P.outerPolynomial s) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing P.completedPolynomialRing :=
    AdicCompletion.isNoetherianRing
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A))
  exact MvPolynomial.isNoetherianRing

/-- `A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y] ≅ B[y]`: a polynomial ring over a quotient. -/
public def outerQuotientEquiv :
    (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s) ≃ₐ[A] MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier :=
  ((MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial
        (σ := Fin s) P.ideal).symm.restrictScalars A).trans
    (MvPolynomial.mapAlgEquiv (Fin s) P.quotientEquiv)

/-- The ideal generated by `I` in `A⟨x⟩[y]`, along which that ring is completed. -/
public abbrev outerAdicIdeal : Ideal (P.outerPolynomial s) :=
  I.map (algebraMap A (P.outerPolynomial s))

/-- The completion `(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` of `A⟨x⟩[y]` along the ideal generated by `I`. -/
public abbrev outerCompletion := AdicCompletion (P.outerAdicIdeal s) (P.outerPolynomial s)

/-- The ideal `J · (A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` of the completion. -/
public abbrev outerCompletionIdeal : Ideal (P.outerCompletion s) :=
  (P.outerIdeal s).map (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerCompletion s))

/-- `A⟨x, y⟩ ≅ (A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩`, the identification of
`AdicCompletion.finIteratedMvPolynomialAlgEquiv` at the presentation's variables. -/
public def combinedIteratedEquiv :
    AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) ≃ₐ[A]
      P.outerCompletion s :=
  AdicCompletion.finIteratedMvPolynomialAlgEquiv I (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing I)
    P.variableCount s

/-- The inclusion `A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩` of the inner variables: the canonical map into
`(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` read through `A⟨x, y⟩ ≅ (A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩`. -/
public def combinedInclusion :
    P.completedPolynomialRing →ₐ[A]
      AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) :=
  (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).symm.toAlgHom.comp
    ((Algebra.ofId P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s)).restrictScalars A)

private theorem combinedIteratedEquiv_combinedInclusion (z : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    P.combinedIteratedEquiv s (P.combinedInclusion s z) =
      algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s) z :=
  (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).apply_symm_apply _

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- The ideal generated by `I` in `B[y]` is the one the presentation `B⟨y⟩` is completed
along. -/
public theorem outerQuotientEquiv_map_adicIdeal :
    AdicCompletion.mvPolynomialIdeal B.adicIdeal (Fin s) =
      ((P.outerAdicIdeal s).map
          (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s))).map
        ((P.outerQuotientEquiv s : _ →+* _)) := by
  have hfactor : (algebraMap A (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)) =
      ((P.outerQuotientEquiv s : _ →+* _)).comp
        ((algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)).comp
          (algebraMap A (P.outerPolynomial s))) := by
    refine RingHom.ext fun a => ?_
    simp only [RingHom.comp_apply]
    rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply]
    exact ((P.outerQuotientEquiv s).commutes a).symm
  calc AdicCompletion.mvPolynomialIdeal B.adicIdeal (Fin s)
      = I.map (algebraMap A (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)) := by
        rw [AdicCompletion.mvPolynomialIdeal, AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.adicIdeal, Ideal.map_map]
        rfl
    _ = _ := by rw [hfactor, ← Ideal.map_map, ← Ideal.map_map]

/-- **Completion commutes with the quotient**: `(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩ ⧸ J·(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩ ≅ B⟨y⟩`.  This is
`adicCompletionQuotientAlgEquiv`, where exactness of `I`-adic completion on finite modules
over the Noetherian ring `A⟨x⟩[y]` enters, followed by `A⟨x⟩[y]/J ≅ B[y]`. -/
public def combinedQuotientEquiv :
    (P.outerCompletion s ⧸ P.outerCompletionIdeal s) ≃ₐ[A]
      AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) :=
  ((adicCompletionQuotientAlgEquiv (P.outerAdicIdeal s)
        (P.outerIdeal s)).restrictScalars A).trans
    (AdicCompletion.congrAlgEquiv (P.outerQuotientEquiv s)
      (P.outerQuotientEquiv_map_adicIdeal s))

/-- **The surjection `π : A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ B⟨y⟩` of Stacks 0ALM.**  It is the quotient map by
`J·(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` read through the identifications `A⟨x, y⟩ ≅ (A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` and
`(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩ ⧸ J ≅ B⟨y⟩`. -/
public def combinedProjection :
    AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) →ₐ[A]
      AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) :=
  (P.combinedQuotientEquiv s).toAlgHom.comp
    ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A (P.outerCompletionIdeal s)).comp
      (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).toAlgHom)

/-- The value of `π` on an element, spelled out. -/
public theorem combinedProjection_apply
    (z : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :
    P.combinedProjection s z =
      P.combinedQuotientEquiv s
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.outerCompletionIdeal s) (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s z)) :=
  rfl

/-- `π` is surjective: it is a quotient map composed with isomorphisms. -/
public theorem combinedProjection_surjective :
    Function.Surjective (P.combinedProjection s) := by
  intro c
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (P.combinedQuotientEquiv s).surjective c
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective z
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).surjective w
  exact ⟨p, by rw [combinedProjection_apply, hp, hw, hz]⟩

/-- **The kernel of `π` is `J · A⟨x, y⟩`.**  The outer identification is injective, so the
kernel is the preimage of the ideal generated by `J` in `(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩`, which is the ideal
generated by `J` in `A⟨x, y⟩`. -/
public theorem ker_combinedProjection :
    RingHom.ker (P.combinedProjection s).toRingHom =
      P.ideal.map (P.combinedInclusion s : P.completedPolynomialRing →+* _) := by
  have hmap : P.outerCompletionIdeal s =
      P.ideal.map (algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s)) := by
    rw [outerCompletionIdeal, outerIdeal, Ideal.map_map, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq]
  have hmem : ∀ z, P.combinedProjection s z = 0 ↔
      (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s) z ∈ P.outerCompletionIdeal s := fun z => by
    rw [combinedProjection_apply, EmbeddingLike.map_eq_zero_iff, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  have hcomp : ((P.combinedInclusion s) : P.completedPolynomialRing →+*
        AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) =
      (((P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).symm : P.outerCompletion s →+*
          AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))).comp
        (algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s)) := rfl
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · intro z hz
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at hz
    have h1 : (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s) z ∈
        P.ideal.map (algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s)) := by
      rw [← hmap]
      exact (hmem z).mp hz
    have h2 := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem
      ((P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).symm : P.outerCompletion s →+*
        AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) h1
    rw [Ideal.map_map, ← hcomp] at h2
    rwa [show ((P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).symm : P.outerCompletion s →+*
          AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
        ((P.combinedIteratedEquiv s) z) = z from
      (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).symm_apply_apply z] at h2
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro j hj
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
    refine (hmem _).mpr ?_
    rw [hmap, RingHom.coe_coe,
      P.combinedIteratedEquiv_combinedInclusion s j]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hj

/-- The inclusion `A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩` is the expected one: it sends the `i`-th inner variable to
the `i`-th variable of `A⟨x, y⟩`.  This is what identifies `combinedInclusion` with the
substitution the source performs, rather than with some other map. -/
public theorem combinedInclusion_of_X (i : Fin P.variableCount) :
    P.combinedInclusion s
        (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) (MvPolynomial.X i)) =
      AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
        (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.castAdd s i)) := by
  have hX : (AdicCompletion.finSumEquiv P.variableCount s).symm (Fin.castAdd s i) =
      Sum.inr i := by
    rw [Equiv.symm_apply_eq]
    simp [AdicCompletion.finSumEquiv]
  have key := AdicCompletion.finIteratedMvPolynomialAlgEquiv_of I
    (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing I) P.variableCount s (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.castAdd s i))
  rw [MvPolynomial.rename_X, hX, AdicCompletion.iterateMvPolynomial_X_inr] at key
  have hright : AdicCompletion.of (P.outerAdicIdeal s) (P.outerPolynomial s)
      (MvPolynomial.C (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A)
        (MvPolynomial.X i))) =
      algebraMap P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerCompletion s)
        (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) (MvPolynomial.X i)) := by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerPolynomial s)
      (P.outerCompletion s), AdicCompletion.algebraMap_apply, Algebra.algebraMap_self_apply]
    rfl
  refine (P.combinedIteratedEquiv s).injective ?_
  rw [P.combinedIteratedEquiv_combinedInclusion s, ← hright]
  exact key.symm

/-- **The combined presentation of Stacks 0ALM.**  Given a surjection of `A`-algebras from
`B⟨y₁, …, y_s⟩` onto an object `C` of (0AL4) — for instance the presenting surjection of a
completed polynomial presentation of `C` over `B` — composing it with `π` presents `C` as a
quotient of `A⟨x₁, …, x_r, y₁, …, y_s⟩`, in `r + s` variables.  This is the presentation
`C = A⟨x, y⟩ / K` of the source. -/
public def combinedPresentation {C : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
    (ψ : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) →ₐ[A] C.carrier)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    CompletedPolynomialPresentation I C where
  variableCount := P.variableCount + s
  ideal := RingHom.ker (ψ.comp (P.combinedProjection s)).toRingHom
  quotientEquiv :=
    Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective (hψ.comp (P.combinedProjection_surjective s))

/-- The combined presentation has `P.variableCount + s` variables: the inner variables of `P`
followed by the `s` outer ones. -/
@[simp] public theorem combinedPresentation_variableCount {C : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
    (ψ : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) →ₐ[A] C.carrier)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    (P.combinedPresentation s ψ hψ).variableCount = P.variableCount + s := rfl

/-- The kernel `K` of the combined presentation is the kernel of `ψ ∘ π`, hence the preimage
under `π` of the kernel `J'` of `ψ`. -/
public theorem ker_combinedPresentation {C : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
    (ψ : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) →ₐ[A] C.carrier)
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) :
    (P.combinedPresentation s ψ hψ).ker =
      Ideal.comap ((P.combinedProjection s).toRingHom) (RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom) := by
  rw [ker_eq_ideal]
  rfl

/-! ## The two morphisms of extensions, and the degree-`1` row of Stacks 0ALM -/

section Extensions

variable {C : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I} [Algebra B.carrier C.carrier]
  [IsScalarTower A B.carrier C.carrier]
  (ψ : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) →ₐ[B.carrier] C.carrier)
  (hψ : Function.Surjective (ψ.restrictScalars A))

/-- If `q ∈ (A⟨x⟩ ⧸ J)[y]` corresponds to the class of `p` in `A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y]`, then `p`
goes to `q` transported along `A⟨x⟩ ⧸ J ≅ B`. -/
private theorem outerQuotientEquiv_eq_map {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    {B : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I} (P : CompletedPolynomialPresentation I B) (s : ℕ)
    {p : P.outerPolynomial s}
    {q : MvPolynomial (Fin s) (P.completedPolynomialRing ⧸ P.ideal)}
    (h : MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial (σ := Fin s) P.ideal q =
      algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s) p) :
    P.outerQuotientEquiv s
        (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s) p) =
      MvPolynomial.mapAlgEquiv (Fin s) P.quotientEquiv q := by
  rw [← h]
  exact congrArg (MvPolynomial.mapAlgEquiv (Fin s) P.quotientEquiv)
    (AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ q)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- The identification `A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y] ≅ B[y]` sends the class of a constant to the
constant of its image. -/
public theorem outerQuotientEquiv_algebraMap_C (z : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    P.outerQuotientEquiv s
        (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)
          (MvPolynomial.C z)) =
      MvPolynomial.C (P.toAlgHom z) := by
  have hfwd : (MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial (σ := Fin s) P.ideal)
      (MvPolynomial.C (Ideal.Quotient.mk P.ideal z)) =
      algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)
        (MvPolynomial.C z) := by
    simp [MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial]
    rfl
  rw [P.outerQuotientEquiv_eq_map s hfwd, MvPolynomial.mapAlgEquiv_apply, MvPolynomial.map_C]
  rfl

/-- `π` sends an element whose image in `(A⟨x⟩)⟨y⟩` is a polynomial `p` to the image of `p`
in `B[y]`, viewed in `B⟨y⟩`. -/
private theorem combinedProjection_of_iterated {z : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I
      (Fin (P.variableCount + s))} {p : P.outerPolynomial s}
    (h : P.combinedIteratedEquiv s z = algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerCompletion s) p) :
    P.combinedProjection s z =
      AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
        (P.outerQuotientEquiv s
          (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s) p)) := by
  rw [combinedProjection_apply, h,
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk (P.outerCompletionIdeal s)
          (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerCompletion s) p) =
        algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s)
          (P.outerCompletion s ⧸ P.outerCompletionIdeal s) p from rfl,
    combinedQuotientEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    show ((adicCompletionQuotientAlgEquiv (P.outerAdicIdeal s)
            (P.outerIdeal s)).restrictScalars A)
          (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s)
            (P.outerCompletion s ⧸ P.outerCompletionIdeal s) p) =
        algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s)
          (AdicCompletion ((P.outerAdicIdeal s).map
            (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)))
            (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)) p from
      (adicCompletionQuotientAlgEquiv (P.outerAdicIdeal s) (P.outerIdeal s)).commutes _,
    AdicCompletion.algebraMap_apply, AdicCompletion.congrAlgEquiv_of]

/-- **`π` restricted to the inner variables is the presenting surjection of `B`.**  That is,
the square

```
A⟨x⟩  ⟶  A⟨x, y⟩
  ↓          ↓
  B    ⟶   B⟨y⟩
```

commutes, which is what makes the inclusion of the inner variables a morphism of
extensions. -/
public theorem combinedProjection_combinedInclusion (z : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    P.combinedProjection s (P.combinedInclusion s z) =
      algebraMap B.carrier (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
        (P.toAlgHom z) := by
  rw [P.combinedProjection_of_iterated s (p := MvPolynomial.C z)
      ((P.combinedIteratedEquiv_combinedInclusion s z).trans
        (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply P.completedPolynomialRing (P.outerPolynomial s)
          (P.outerCompletion s) z)),
    outerQuotientEquiv_algebraMap_C,
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B.carrier (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)),
    AdicCompletion.algebraMap_apply, Algebra.algebraMap_self_apply]
  rfl

/-- The presenting surjection of the combined presentation is `ψ ∘ π`. -/
public theorem combinedPresentation_toAlgHom :
    (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom =
      (ψ.restrictScalars A).comp (P.combinedProjection s) :=
  AlgHom.ext fun _ => rfl

/-- The inclusion of the inner variables as a morphism of extensions
`(A⟨x⟩ ↠ B) ⟶ (A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ C)`. -/
public def innerExtensionHom :
    P.extension.Hom (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension where
  toRingHom := (P.combinedInclusion s).toRingHom
  toRingHom_algebraMap a := (P.combinedInclusion s).commutes a
  algebraMap_toRingHom z :=
    (congrArg ψ (P.combinedProjection_combinedInclusion s z)).trans (ψ.commutes _)

/-- The ring map underlying `innerExtensionHom` is the inclusion `combinedInclusion` of the
inner variables. -/
@[simp] public theorem innerExtensionHom_toRingHom :
    (P.innerExtensionHom s ψ hψ).toRingHom = (P.combinedInclusion s).toRingHom := rfl

/-- The projection `π` as a morphism of extensions `(A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ C) ⟶ (B⟨y⟩ ↠ C)`. -/
public def outerExtensionHom :
    (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension.Hom
      (Algebra.Extension.ofSurjective ψ hψ) where
  toRingHom := (P.combinedProjection s).toRingHom
  toRingHom_algebraMap a :=
    ((P.combinedProjection s).commutes a).trans
      (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B.carrier
        (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) a)
  algebraMap_toRingHom _ := rfl

/-- The ring map underlying `outerExtensionHom` is the projection `π = combinedProjection`. -/
@[simp] public theorem outerExtensionHom_toRingHom :
    (P.outerExtensionHom s ψ hψ).toRingHom = (P.combinedProjection s).toRingHom := rfl

/-- **The degree-`1` row of Stacks 0ALM for the completed cotangent complexes.**  For a
presentation `B = A⟨x⟩/J`, a presentation `C = B⟨y⟩/J'` and the combined presentation
`C = A⟨x, y⟩/K`, the sequence

```
C ⊗_B J/J²  ⟶  K/K²  ⟶  J'/(J')²  ⟶  0
```

is exact, the maps being those induced by the inclusion of the inner variables and by `π`.
This is the row that the snake lemma of
`NaiveCotangent.exists_sixTerm_exact_of_finAppend` takes as input; the hypothesis
`ker π = J·A⟨x, y⟩` it rests on is
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.ker_combinedProjection`. -/
public theorem exact_cotangentMap_combined :
    Function.Exact
      ((Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
        (P.innerExtensionHom s ψ hψ)).liftBaseChange C.carrier)
      (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map (P.outerExtensionHom s ψ hψ)) := by
  have hk : Algebra.Extension.ker P.extension = P.ideal := P.ker_eq_ideal
  refine Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.exact_liftBaseChange_map_of_ker_eq _ _
    (P.combinedProjection_surjective s) ?_
  rw [hk, outerExtensionHom_toRingHom, innerExtensionHom_toRingHom]
  exact P.ker_combinedProjection s

/-- The right-hand map of the degree-`1` row is surjective. -/
public theorem surjective_cotangentMap_combined :
    Function.Surjective
      (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map (P.outerExtensionHom s ψ hψ)) :=
  Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.surjective_map_of_surjective_toRingHom _
    (P.combinedProjection_surjective s)

end Extensions

/-! ## `π` and the inclusion are continuous

Both maps are *induced* maps of adic completions: each is the completion of a map of
polynomial algebras which carries the coefficient ideal into the coefficient ideal.  Once that
is known — and `AdicCompletion.algHom_ext_of_of` reduces knowing it to the values on
polynomials, which `combinedInclusion_of_X` and `combinedProjection_of_X_natAdd` supply —
continuity for the inverse-limit topologies is `Rig.continuous_algHomOfMapPowLe`.
-/

section Continuity

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- The identification `A⟨x⟩[y] ⧸ J·A⟨x⟩[y] ≅ B[y]` fixes the outer variables. -/
public theorem outerQuotientEquiv_algebraMap_X (j : Fin s) :
    P.outerQuotientEquiv s
        (algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)
          (MvPolynomial.X j)) =
      MvPolynomial.X j := by
  have hfwd : (MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial (σ := Fin s) P.ideal)
      (MvPolynomial.X j) =
      algebraMap (P.outerPolynomial s) (P.outerPolynomial s ⧸ P.outerIdeal s)
        (MvPolynomial.X j) := by
    simp [MvPolynomial.quotientEquivQuotientMvPolynomial]
    rfl
  rw [P.outerQuotientEquiv_eq_map s hfwd, MvPolynomial.mapAlgEquiv_apply, MvPolynomial.map_X]

/-- **`π` sends the `j`-th outer variable to the `j`-th variable of `B⟨y⟩`.**  Together with
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedProjection_combinedInclusion`, which handles the
inner variables, this pins `π` down on all of `A⟨x, y⟩`. -/
public theorem combinedProjection_of_X_natAdd (j : Fin s) :
    P.combinedProjection s
        (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j))) =
      AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier) (MvPolynomial.X j) := by
  have hX : (AdicCompletion.finSumEquiv P.variableCount s).symm
      (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j) = Sum.inl j := by
    rw [Equiv.symm_apply_eq]
    simp [AdicCompletion.finSumEquiv]
  have key := AdicCompletion.finIteratedMvPolynomialAlgEquiv_of I
    (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing I) P.variableCount s
    (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j))
  rw [MvPolynomial.rename_X, hX, AdicCompletion.iterateMvPolynomial_X_inl] at key
  rw [P.combinedProjection_of_iterated s (p := MvPolynomial.X j) key,
    outerQuotientEquiv_algebraMap_X]

/-- **The polynomial map underlying `π`**: the `A`-algebra map
`A[x, y] → B[y]` which sends an inner variable `xᵢ` to the constant given by its image in `B`
and an outer variable `yⱼ` to `yⱼ`.  The surjection `π` is its completion. -/
public def outerPolynomialMap :
    MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A →ₐ[A] MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval (Fin.addCases
    (fun i : Fin P.variableCount => MvPolynomial.C (P.toAlgHom
      (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) (MvPolynomial.X i))))
    (fun j : Fin s => (MvPolynomial.X j : MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)))

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- `outerPolynomialMap` sends each inner variable `xᵢ` to the constant given by its image in
`B`. -/
@[simp] public theorem outerPolynomialMap_X_castAdd (i : Fin P.variableCount) :
    P.outerPolynomialMap s (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.castAdd s i)) =
      MvPolynomial.C (P.toAlgHom
        (AdicCompletion.of _ (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) (MvPolynomial.X i))) := by
  simp [outerPolynomialMap]

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- `outerPolynomialMap` sends each outer variable `yⱼ` to `yⱼ`. -/
@[simp] public theorem outerPolynomialMap_X_natAdd (j : Fin s) :
    P.outerPolynomialMap s (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)) =
      MvPolynomial.X j := by
  simp [outerPolynomialMap]

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- The polynomial map underlying `π` is an `A`-algebra map, so it fixes constants. -/
public theorem outerPolynomialMap_C (a : A) :
    P.outerPolynomialMap s (MvPolynomial.C a) =
      MvPolynomial.C (algebraMap A B.carrier a) := by
  rw [show (MvPolynomial.C a : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) =
      algebraMap A (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) a from rfl,
    AlgHom.commutes,
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B.carrier (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)]
  rfl

/-- The inclusion of the inner variables agrees on polynomials with the renaming
`A[x] → A[x, y]`. -/
public theorem combinedInclusion_algebraMap (p : MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) :
    P.combinedInclusion s
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) P.completedPolynomialRing p) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
        (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
        (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd s) p) := by
  have key : (P.combinedInclusion s).comp
        (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A)
          P.completedPolynomialRing) =
      (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))).comp
        (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd s)) := by
    refine MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun i => ?_
    simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, IsScalarTower.coe_toAlgHom', MvPolynomial.rename_X]
    exact P.combinedInclusion_of_X s i
  exact congr($key p)

/-- `π` agrees on polynomials with `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.outerPolynomialMap`. -/
public theorem combinedProjection_algebraMap
    (p : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) :
    P.combinedProjection s
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) p) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
        (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
        (P.outerPolynomialMap s p) := by
  have key : (P.combinedProjection s).comp
        (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))) =
      (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))).comp
        (P.outerPolynomialMap s) := by
    refine MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun k => ?_
    simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, IsScalarTower.coe_toAlgHom']
    refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun j => ?_) k
    · rw [outerPolynomialMap_X_castAdd,
        show algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
              (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
              (MvPolynomial.X (Fin.castAdd s i)) =
            P.combinedInclusion s (AdicCompletion.of _
              (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) (MvPolynomial.X i)) from
          (P.combinedInclusion_of_X s i).symm,
        P.combinedProjection_combinedInclusion s,
        IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B.carrier (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))]
      rfl
    · rw [outerPolynomialMap_X_natAdd]
      exact P.combinedProjection_of_X_natAdd s j
  exact congr($key p)

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- Renaming the inner variables carries the coefficient ideal into the coefficient ideal. -/
public theorem map_pow_rename_castAdd_le :
    ((I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A)) ^ 1).map
        (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd s) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A →ₐ[A]
            MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) ≤
      I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) := by
  rw [pow_one, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro a ha
  simp only [Ideal.mem_comap, MvPolynomial.rename_C]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- The polynomial map underlying `π` carries the coefficient ideal of `A[x, y]` into the
coefficient ideal of `B[y]`. -/
public theorem map_pow_outerPolynomialMap_le :
    ((I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)) ^ 1).map
        (P.outerPolynomialMap s) ≤
      B.adicIdeal.map (MvPolynomial.C : B.carrier →+* MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier) := by
  rw [pow_one, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro a ha
  simp only [Ideal.mem_comap]
  rw [show ((P.outerPolynomialMap s) ((MvPolynomial.C : A →+* _) a)) =
      MvPolynomial.C (algebraMap A B.carrier a) from P.outerPolynomialMap_C s a]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)

/-- **The inclusion of the inner variables is the completion of the renaming
`A[x] → A[x, y]`.**  Both maps agree on polynomials, so
`AdicCompletion.algHom_ext_of_of` identifies them. -/
public theorem combinedInclusion_eq :
    P.combinedInclusion s =
      AdicCompletion.algHomOfMapPowLe A
        (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd s) :
          MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A →ₐ[A]
            MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
        (P.map_pow_rename_castAdd_le s) :=
  AdicCompletion.algHom_ext_of_of A
    (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A))
    ((Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing I).map
      (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A))
    (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A))
    (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd s)) (P.map_pow_rename_castAdd_le s) _ _
    (fun p => P.combinedInclusion_algebraMap s p)
    (fun p => AdicCompletion.algHomOfMapPowLe_of A _ _ p)

/-- **`π` is the completion of `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.outerPolynomialMap`.** -/
public theorem combinedProjection_eq :
    P.combinedProjection s =
      AdicCompletion.algHomOfMapPowLe A (P.outerPolynomialMap s)
        (P.map_pow_outerPolynomialMap_le s) :=
  AdicCompletion.algHom_ext_of_of A
    (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A))
    ((Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing I).map
      (MvPolynomial.C : A →+* MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A))
    (B.adicIdeal.map (MvPolynomial.C : B.carrier →+* MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier))
    (P.outerPolynomialMap s) (P.map_pow_outerPolynomialMap_le s) _ _
    (fun p => P.combinedProjection_algebraMap s p)
    (fun p => AdicCompletion.algHomOfMapPowLe_of A _ _ p)

/-- **The inclusion `A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩` is continuous** for the inverse-limit topologies. -/
public theorem continuous_combinedInclusion :
    @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin P.variableCount))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I
        (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (P.combinedInclusion s) := by
  rw [P.combinedInclusion_eq s]
  exact Rig.continuous_algHomOfMapPowLe _ (P.map_pow_rename_castAdd_le s)

/-- **The surjection `π : A⟨x, y⟩ ↠ B⟨y⟩` is continuous** for the inverse-limit
topologies. -/
public theorem continuous_combinedProjection :
    @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I
        (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
      (P.combinedProjection s) := by
  rw [P.combinedProjection_eq s]
  exact Rig.continuous_algHomOfMapPowLe _ (P.map_pow_outerPolynomialMap_le s)

end Continuity

/-! ## The `partialDeriv` compatibilities

`Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex.partialDeriv_unique` quantifies over derivations of `A⟨x⟩`
into **itself**, so it cannot compare the derivations `A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩` and
`A⟨x, y⟩ → B⟨y⟩` which the two squares of Stacks 0ALM involve.  What replaces it is the
density argument in the reusable form `Rig.eq_of_continuous_of_algebraMap`, fed by the
continuity results above.
-/

section Derivations

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- **An outer variable does not occur in a polynomial in the inner variables**: the formal
partial derivative `∂/∂y_j` kills the image of `A[x] → A[x, y]`. -/
public theorem _root_.Rig.pderiv_natAdd_rename_castAdd {r t : ℕ} (j : Fin t)
    (p : MvPolynomial (Fin r) A) :
    MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.natAdd r j) (MvPolynomial.rename (Fin.castAdd t) p) = 0 := by
  classical
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a => simp
  | add p q hp hq => simp [hp, hq]
  | mul_X p k h =>
    have hne : (Fin.castAdd t k : Fin (r + t)) ≠ Fin.natAdd r j := by
      intro hk
      have := congrArg Fin.val hk
      simp [Fin.castAdd, Fin.natAdd] at this
      omega
    simp [h, hne]

omit [IsNoetherianRing A] in
/-- **The chain rule for the polynomial map underlying `π`**: it carries `∂/∂y_j` of `A[x, y]`
to `∂/∂y_j` of `B[y]`.  The inner variables go to constants, which `∂/∂y_j` kills, and the
outer variables go to themselves. -/
public theorem pderiv_outerPolynomialMap (j : Fin s)
    (p : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A) :
    MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.outerPolynomialMap s p) =
      P.outerPolynomialMap s
        (MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j) p) := by
  classical
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a => simp [P.outerPolynomialMap_C s a]
  | add p q hp hq => simp [hp, hq]
  | mul_X p k h =>
    have hk : MvPolynomial.pderiv j (P.outerPolynomialMap s (MvPolynomial.X k)) =
        P.outerPolynomialMap s
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j) (MvPolynomial.X k)) := by
      refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun j' => ?_) k
      · have hne : (Fin.castAdd s i : Fin (P.variableCount + s)) ≠
            Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j := by
          intro hc
          have hv := congrArg Fin.val hc
          simp [Fin.castAdd, Fin.natAdd] at hv
          omega
        simp [hne]
      · by_cases hjj : j' = j
        · subst hjj
          simp
        · have hne : (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j' : Fin (P.variableCount + s)) ≠
              Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j := fun hc => hjj ((Fin.natAdd_inj _).mp hc)
          simp [hne, hjj]
    simp only [map_mul, Derivation.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, map_add, hk, h]

/-- **The first `partialDeriv` compatibility of Stacks 0ALM**: the inclusion of the inner
variables intertwines `∂^P/∂xᵢ` on `A⟨x⟩` with `∂^{comb}/∂x_{castAdd i}` on `A⟨x, y⟩`.

`Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex.partialDeriv_unique` cannot be used here: its field
quantifies over derivations of `A⟨x⟩` *into itself*, whereas the square compares derivations
`A⟨x⟩ → A⟨x, y⟩`.  Instead both composites are continuous, by
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.continuous_combinedInclusion`, and agree on polynomials
by `MvPolynomial.pderiv_rename`, so `Rig.eq_of_continuous_of_algebraMap` applies. -/
public theorem partialDeriv_combinedInclusion (i : Fin P.variableCount)
    (D : Derivation A P.completedPolynomialRing P.completedPolynomialRing)
    (E : Derivation A (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))))
    (hD : @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin P.variableCount))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin P.variableCount)) D)
    (hE : @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) E)
    (hDp : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A,
      D (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) P.completedPolynomialRing p) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin P.variableCount) A) P.completedPolynomialRing
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv i p))
    (hEp : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A,
      E (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) p) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.castAdd s i) p))
    (x : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    P.combinedInclusion s (D x) = E (P.combinedInclusion s x) := by
  let _ : TopologicalSpace P.completedPolynomialRing :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin P.variableCount)
  let _ : TopologicalSpace
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  let _ : TopologicalSpace (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  have _ : T2Space (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)
  have _ : T2Space (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)
  have hfun : (fun y => P.combinedInclusion s (D y)) =
      (fun y => E (P.combinedInclusion s y)) := by
    refine Rig.eq_of_continuous_of_algebraMap I P.variableCount _ _
      ((P.continuous_combinedInclusion s).comp hD)
      (hE.comp (P.continuous_combinedInclusion s)) fun p => ?_
    change P.combinedInclusion s (D (algebraMap _ _ p)) =
      E (P.combinedInclusion s (algebraMap _ _ p))
    rw [hDp, P.combinedInclusion_algebraMap, P.combinedInclusion_algebraMap, hEp,
      MvPolynomial.pderiv_rename (Fin.castAdd_injective ..) i p]
  exact congrFun hfun x

/-- **The second `partialDeriv` compatibility of Stacks 0ALM**: `∂^{comb}/∂y_j` kills the image
of `A⟨x⟩` in `A⟨x, y⟩`.  This is what makes the left-hand square of the diagram commute over
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.finInl`, whose last `s` coordinates are zero. -/
public theorem partialDeriv_natAdd_combinedInclusion (j : Fin s)
    (E : Derivation A (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))))
    (hE : @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) E)
    (hEp : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A,
      E (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) p) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j) p))
    (x : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    E (P.combinedInclusion s x) = 0 := by
  let _ : TopologicalSpace P.completedPolynomialRing :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin P.variableCount)
  let _ : TopologicalSpace
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  let _ : TopologicalSpace (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  have _ : T2Space (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)
  have _ : T2Space (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)
  have hfun : (fun y => E (P.combinedInclusion s y)) =
      (fun _ : P.completedPolynomialRing =>
        (0 : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))) := by
    refine Rig.eq_of_continuous_of_algebraMap I P.variableCount _ _
      (hE.comp (P.continuous_combinedInclusion s)) continuous_const fun p => ?_
    change E (P.combinedInclusion s (algebraMap _ _ p)) = 0
    rw [P.combinedInclusion_algebraMap, hEp, pderiv_natAdd_rename_castAdd (A := A) j p, map_zero]
  exact congrFun hfun x

/-- **The third `partialDeriv` compatibility of Stacks 0ALM**: `π` intertwines
`∂^{comb}/∂y_j` on `A⟨x, y⟩` with `∂^Q/∂y_j` on `B⟨y⟩`.  Both composites are continuous, by
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.continuous_combinedProjection`, and agree on polynomials
by the chain rule `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.pderiv_outerPolynomialMap`. -/
public theorem partialDeriv_combinedProjection (j : Fin s)
    (E : Derivation A (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))))
    (F : Derivation B.carrier
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)))
    (hE : @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) E)
    (hF : @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) F)
    (hEp : ∀ p : MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A,
      E (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) p) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin (P.variableCount + s)) A)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s)))
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j) p))
    (hFp : ∀ q : MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier,
      F (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) q) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv j q))
    (x : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :
    P.combinedProjection s (E x) = F (P.combinedProjection s x) := by
  let _ : TopologicalSpace
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  let _ : TopologicalSpace (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra I (P.variableCount + s)) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology I (Fin (P.variableCount + s))
  let _ : TopologicalSpace
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s)
  let _ : TopologicalSpace (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra B.adicIdeal s) :=
    RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s)
  have _ : T2Space (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra B.adicIdeal s
  have _ : T2Space (Rig.completedPolynomialAlgebra B.adicIdeal s) :=
    Rig.t2Space_completedPolynomialAlgebra B.adicIdeal s
  have hfun : (fun y => P.combinedProjection s (E y)) =
      (fun y => F (P.combinedProjection s y)) := by
    refine Rig.eq_of_continuous_of_algebraMap I (P.variableCount + s) _ _
      ((P.continuous_combinedProjection s).comp hE)
      (hF.comp (P.continuous_combinedProjection s)) fun p => ?_
    change P.combinedProjection s (E (algebraMap _ _ p)) =
      F (P.combinedProjection s (algebraMap _ _ p))
    rw [hEp, P.combinedProjection_algebraMap, P.combinedProjection_algebraMap, hFp,
      P.pderiv_outerPolynomialMap s j p]
  exact congrFun hfun x

end Derivations

/-! ## `H⁰` commutes with base change

Stacks 0ALM's display is asymmetric in spelling: the `H⁻¹` row's first entry is
`H⁻¹(NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C)`, with the tensor *inside*, while the `H⁰` row's first entry is
`C ⊗_B H⁰(NL^∧_{B/A})`, with the tensor *outside*.  The complex the source works with is the
base-changed one in both rows — its proof opens by observing that `NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C` makes
sense — so the outside spelling is a display convenience, justified by the fact that `H⁰` is a
cokernel and that the tensor product is right exact.  This section records that identification,
so that the display's reading of the `H⁰` entry is recoverable by name.
-/

section BaseChangeCokernel

/-- **`H⁰` commutes with base change.**  For a two-term complex `d : M → ⨁_{i<n} R` of
`R`-modules and an `R`-algebra `S`,

```
S ⊗_R (⨁_{i<n} R ⧸ im d)  ≅  ⨁_{i<n} S ⧸ im (S ⊗_R d),
```

the tensor product passing from outside the cokernel to inside it.  This holds with no
hypotheses: `H⁰` is a cokernel and the tensor product is right exact, which is
`lTensor_exact` applied to `M → ⨁_{i<n} R → coker d → 0`, and the free term is identified by
`TensorProduct.piScalarRight`. -/
public noncomputable def _root_.Rig.tensorProductH0Equiv {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {n : ℕ}
    (d : M →ₗ[R] (Fin n → R)) :
    TensorProduct R S ((Fin n → R) ⧸ LinearMap.range d) ≃ₗ[S]
      ((Fin n → S) ⧸ LinearMap.range
        ((((Algebra.linearMap R S).compLeft (Fin n)) ∘ₗ d).liftBaseChange S)) := by
  classical
  have hgsurj : Function.Surjective
      ((Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d)).baseChange S) :=
    LinearMap.baseChange_surjective S (Submodule.mkQ_surjective _)
  have hb := (lTensor_exact S (LinearMap.exact_map_mkQ_range d)
    (Submodule.mkQ_surjective (LinearMap.range d))).linearMap_ker_eq
  have hker : LinearMap.ker ((Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d)).baseChange S) =
      LinearMap.range (d.baseChange S) := by
    refine Submodule.ext fun x => ?_
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.mem_range]
    constructor
    · intro hx
      have hx' : x ∈ LinearMap.ker
          (LinearMap.lTensor S (Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d))) := by
        rw [LinearMap.mem_ker,
          ← congrFun (LinearMap.baseChange_eq_lTensor
            (A := S) (Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d))) x]
        exact hx
      rw [hb, LinearMap.mem_range] at hx'
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hx'
      exact ⟨y, (congrFun (LinearMap.baseChange_eq_lTensor (A := S) d) y).trans hy⟩
    · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
      have hmem : (LinearMap.lTensor S d) y ∈ LinearMap.ker
          (LinearMap.lTensor S (Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d))) := by
        rw [hb]
        exact ⟨y, rfl⟩
      rw [congrFun (LinearMap.baseChange_eq_lTensor (A := S) d) y,
        congrFun (LinearMap.baseChange_eq_lTensor
          (A := S) (Submodule.mkQ (LinearMap.range d))) _]
      exact LinearMap.mem_ker.mp hmem
  have hE : (TensorProduct.piScalarRight R S S (Fin n)).toLinearMap ∘ₗ (d.baseChange S) =
      (((Algebra.linearMap R S).compLeft (Fin n)) ∘ₗ d).liftBaseChange S := by
    refine TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.curry_injective ?_
    refine LinearMap.ext fun c => LinearMap.ext fun m => ?_
    funext j
    simp [TensorProduct.piScalarRightHom_tmul, Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm]
  exact (LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective _ hgsurj).symm.trans
    ((Submodule.quotEquivOfEq _ _ hker).trans
      (Submodule.Quotient.equiv _ _ (TensorProduct.piScalarRight R S S (Fin n))
        (by rw [← LinearMap.range_comp]; exact congrArg LinearMap.range hE)))

end BaseChangeCokernel

/-! ## The six-term exact sequence

With the two squares in hand, every input of
`NaiveCotangent.exists_sixTerm_exact_of_finAppend` is available: the degree-`0` row is its own
split row, the degree-`1` row is `exact_cotangentMap_combined` together with
`surjective_cotangentMap_combined`, and the two squares are
`combinedDifferential_comp_innerCotangentMap` and `outerDifferential_comp_outerCotangentMap`.
-/

section SixTerm

variable {C : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I} [Algebra B.carrier C.carrier]
  [IsScalarTower A B.carrier C.carrier]
  (ψ : AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s) →ₐ[B.carrier] C.carrier)
  (hψ : Function.Surjective (ψ.restrictScalars A))

/-- **The degree-`0` differential of `NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C`**, the complex `X` of Stacks 0ALM: the
base change along `B → C` of `J/J² → ⨁_{i<r} B dxᵢ`.  It is the one-line `liftBaseChange` of
the differential of `NL^∧_{B/A}` followed by `algebraMap B C` componentwise. -/
public noncomputable def innerBaseChangeDifferential (KB : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P) :
    TensorProduct B.carrier C.carrier P.extension.Cotangent →ₗ[C.carrier]
      (Fin P.variableCount → C.carrier) :=
  ((((Algebra.linearMap B.carrier C.carrier).compLeft (Fin P.variableCount)) :
      (Fin P.variableCount → B.carrier) →ₗ[B.carrier]
        (Fin P.variableCount → C.carrier)).comp KB.differential).liftBaseChange C.carrier

/-- **The `H⁰` entry of Stacks 0ALM in the source's own spelling.**  The display of 0ALM writes
the first entry of its `H⁰` row as `C ⊗_B H⁰(NL^∧_{B/A})`, with the tensor outside, while
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.exists_sixTerm_exact_combined` has
`H⁰(NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C)`, with it inside — which is the form the connecting map is produced in.
This is the identification between the two, a one-line specialization of
`Rig.tensorProductH0Equiv`.  It is deliberately **untagged**: it is an identification used in
reading 0ALM, not part of 0ALM's covering set. -/
public noncomputable def innerBaseChangeH0Equiv (KB : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P) :
    TensorProduct B.carrier C.carrier
        ((Fin P.variableCount → B.carrier) ⧸ LinearMap.range KB.differential) ≃ₗ[C.carrier]
      NaiveCotangent.H₀
        (NaiveCotangent.TwoTerm.ofFree (P.innerBaseChangeDifferential (C := C) KB)) :=
  Rig.tensorProductH0Equiv KB.differential

/-- **The degree-`0` differential of `NL^∧_{C/B}`**, the complex `Z` of Stacks 0ALM: it sends
the class of `g ∈ J'` to the tuple of the images in `C` of the formal partial derivatives
`∂g/∂yⱼ`.  The derivations `F` are the formal partial derivatives of `B⟨y⟩` over `B`; they are
taken as data because, by `Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex.partialDeriv_unique`, the
continuity and polynomial hypotheses below determine them. -/
public noncomputable def outerDifferential
    (F : Fin s → Derivation B.carrier
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
      (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))) :
    (Algebra.Extension.ofSurjective ψ hψ).Cotangent →ₗ[C.carrier] (Fin s → C.carrier) :=
  LinearMap.pi fun j =>
    cotangentMapOfDerivation (Algebra.Extension.ofSurjective ψ hψ) (F j)

/-- **The degree-`0` differential of `NL^∧_{C/A}`**, the complex `Y` of Stacks 0ALM, with its
target spelled `Fin (r + s) → C` rather than `Fin (combined).variableCount → C`.  The two are
definitionally equal — `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.combinedPresentation_variableCount`
holds by `rfl` — but only the first makes the `Fin.append` splitting of the degree-`0` row
syntactically applicable. -/
public noncomputable def combinedDifferential
    (KC : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ)) :
    (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension.Cotangent →ₗ[C.carrier]
      (Fin (P.variableCount + s) → C.carrier) :=
  KC.differential

/-- The differential of `NL^∧_{C/A}` on the class of `g ∈ K`: the tuple of the images in `C` of
the formal partial derivatives `∂g/∂x_k`, `k` running over all `r + s` variables. -/
public theorem combinedDifferential_mk
    (KC : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ))
    (g : (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension.ker) :
    P.combinedDifferential s ψ hψ KC (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk g) =
      fun k : Fin (P.variableCount + s) =>
        (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom
          (KC.partialDeriv k g.1) :=
  KC.differential_mk g

/-- The presenting surjection of the combined presentation restricted along the inclusion of
the inner variables is the presenting surjection of `B` followed by `B → C`.  This is the
`algebraMap_toRingHom` field of
`Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.innerExtensionHom`, read off. -/
public theorem toAlgHom_combinedInclusion (z : P.completedPolynomialRing) :
    (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom
        (P.combinedInclusion s z) =
      algebraMap B.carrier C.carrier (P.toAlgHom z) :=
  (P.innerExtensionHom s ψ hψ).algebraMap_toRingHom z

variable (KB : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P)
  (KC : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ))

/-- **The left-hand square of Stacks 0ALM commutes.**  The map `C ⊗_B J/J² → K/K²` induced by
the inclusion of the inner variables, followed by the differential of `NL^∧_{C/A}`, is the
differential of `NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C` followed by extension of a tuple by zeros.  Componentwise
this is the first `partialDeriv` compatibility in the inner coordinates and the second in the
outer ones. -/
public theorem combinedDifferential_comp_innerCotangentMap :
    P.combinedDifferential s ψ hψ KC ∘ₗ
        ((Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map
          (P.innerExtensionHom s ψ hψ)).liftBaseChange C.carrier) =
      NaiveCotangent.finInl C.carrier P.variableCount s ∘ₗ
        P.innerBaseChangeDifferential (C := C) KB := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun z => ?_
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply]
  induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add z w hz hw => simp only [map_add]; rw [hz, hw]
  | tmul c x =>
    obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk_surjective (P := P.extension) x
    rw [LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul, Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map_mk, map_smul,
      innerBaseChangeDifferential, LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul, map_smul,
      P.combinedDifferential_mk s ψ hψ KC, LinearMap.comp_apply, KB.differential_mk]
    congr 1
    funext k
    refine Fin.addCases (fun i => ?_) (fun j => ?_) k
    · rw [NaiveCotangent.finInl_apply_castAdd]
      change (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom
          (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.castAdd s i)
            (P.combinedInclusion s (g : P.extension.ker).1)) = _
      have h1 := P.partialDeriv_combinedInclusion s i (KB.partialDeriv i)
        (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.castAdd s i)) (KB.partialDeriv_continuous i)
        (KC.partialDeriv_continuous (Fin.castAdd s i)) (KB.partialDeriv_polynomial i)
        (KC.partialDeriv_polynomial (Fin.castAdd s i)) (g : P.extension.ker).1
      exact (congrArg (fun z => (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom z)
        h1.symm).trans (P.toAlgHom_combinedInclusion s ψ hψ _)
    · rw [NaiveCotangent.finInl_apply_natAdd]
      change (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom
          (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)
            (P.combinedInclusion s (g : P.extension.ker).1)) = _
      have h2 := P.partialDeriv_natAdd_combinedInclusion s j
        (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j))
        (KC.partialDeriv_continuous (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j))
        (KC.partialDeriv_polynomial (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j))
        (g : P.extension.ker).1
      exact (congrArg (fun z => (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).toAlgHom z)
        h2).trans (map_zero _)

variable (F : Fin s → Derivation B.carrier
    (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
    (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)))

/-- **The right-hand square of Stacks 0ALM commutes.**  The map `K/K² → J'/(J')²` induced by
`π`, followed by the differential of `NL^∧_{C/B}`, is the differential of `NL^∧_{C/A}` followed
by projection onto the last `s` coordinates.  Componentwise this is the third `partialDeriv`
compatibility. -/
public theorem outerDifferential_comp_outerCotangentMap
    (hFc : ∀ j, @Continuous _ _
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
      (RestrictedPowerSeries.polynomialCompletionLimitTopology B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) (F j))
    (hFp : ∀ (j : Fin s) (q : MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier),
      F j (algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s)) q) =
        algebraMap (MvPolynomial (Fin s) B.carrier)
          (AdicCompletion.completedMvPolynomial B.adicIdeal (Fin s))
          (MvPolynomial.pderiv j q)) :
    outerDifferential s ψ hψ F ∘ₗ
        (Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map (P.outerExtensionHom s ψ hψ)) =
      NaiveCotangent.finProj C.carrier P.variableCount s ∘ₗ
        P.combinedDifferential s ψ hψ KC := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply]
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk_surjective
    (P := (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension) x
  rw [Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.map_mk, P.combinedDifferential_mk s ψ hψ KC]
  funext j
  refine (cotangentMapOfDerivation_mk (Algebra.Extension.ofSurjective ψ hψ)
    (F j) _).trans ?_
  change ψ (F j (P.combinedProjection s (g : (P.combinedPresentation s
      (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension.ker).1)) =
    ψ (P.combinedProjection s (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)
      (g : (P.combinedPresentation s (ψ.restrictScalars A) hψ).extension.ker).1))
  exact congrArg ψ (P.partialDeriv_combinedProjection s j
    (KC.partialDeriv (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)) (F j)
    (KC.partialDeriv_continuous (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)) (hFc j)
    (KC.partialDeriv_polynomial (Fin.natAdd P.variableCount j)) (hFp j) _).symm

/-- **The six-term exact sequence of Stacks 0ALM.**

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, `I ⊆ A` an ideal, `B` an object of (Stacks 0AL4) with a completed
polynomial presentation `B = A⟨x₁, …, x_r⟩/J`, and `C` an object of (0AL4) over `B` presented
over `B` by `ψ : B⟨y₁, …, y_s⟩ ↠ C`, so that `C = A⟨x, y⟩/K` by the combined presentation.
Then there is an exact sequence

```
H⁻¹(NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B C) → H⁻¹(NL^∧_{C/A}) → H⁻¹(NL^∧_{C/B}) --δ-->
